Then connect committed database CDC events to Jimmer’s `BinLog`, including product/category row changes and association/FK changes. The CDC event must be acknowledged only after invalidation succeeds.

After a Jimmer product update, Jimmer emits an entity-change event. The object cache entry for that `Product` and affected association entries are invalidated in both Caffeine and Redis. The next transparent entity/fetcher load reads fresh data and repopulates the tiers. No repository-level manual cache reads are required.

